QuestGuidance.Register("en",136,{
[4321]="7001E986\n1\tDefeat Fotak\030Defeat Orcs at Ânug-stazg (total: 10)\tFotak and his minions may be found at Ânug-stazg, due east of Mithechad. Perindúr has asked you to defeat the Orc Fotak and his warriors.\n2\tTalk to Perindúr at Mithechad\tPerindúr is at Mithechad, west of Ânug-stazg. You should tell Perindúr of your victory over the Enemy forces at Ânug-stazg.\n",
[4322]="7001E7EA\n1\tDefeat sorcerers (total: 15)\030Defeat Lidognir\tThe ruins of Sâd Doldúr lie south and down the mountain pass from Barad Angol. Faerchiril has asked you to travel to Sâd Doldúr, climb to the upper reaches of the ruins, and defeat Lidognir and his men.\n2\tTalk to Faerchiril at Barad Angol\tFaerchiril is at Barad Angol, north and up the hill from Sâd Doldúr. You should speak with Faerchiril and let her know that Lidognir has been stopped and that his men have been defeated.\n",
[4323]="70042F2D\n1\tDisrupt the forces gathered at Barad Nemorn\tBarad Nemorn is located near where the Morgulduin meets the Anduin in Southern Ithilien. You should enter the Morgul camp at Barad Nemorn to discover what the Orcs there are plotting.\n2\tComplete Quest, Barad Nemorn: Vile Leaders\030Complete Quest, Barad Nemorn: Warg Masters\030Complete Quest, Barad Nemorn: Morgul Warriors\030Complete Quest, Barad Nemorn: Statues of the Dark Lord\030Complete Quest, Barad Nemorn: Troll Teeth\030Search for any orders\tBarad Nemorn is located near where the Morgulduin meets the Anduin in Southern Ithilien. You should destroy any orders from Minus Morgul in Barad Nemorn, and do anything else you can to thwart the enemy's plans.\n3\tTake the orders to Arodor\tFaramir's Look-out is located south-east of Osgiliath. You should give the orders you found in Barad Nemorn to a Ranger at Faramir's Look-out.\n",
[4324]="70042EBE\n1\tDisrupt the forces gathered at Harlanc\tHarlanc is located south of Bâr Húrin. You should enter the Haradrim camp at Harlanc.\n2\tComplete Quest, Harlanc: Half-trolls\030Complete Quest, Harlanc: Haradrim Captains\030Complete Quest, Harlanc: Ranger Caches\030Complete Quest, Harlanc: Haradrim Sashes\030Destroy Haradrim supplies (total: 6)\tHarlanc is located south of Bâr Húrin. You should destroy Haradrim supplies in Harlanc and search for other ways to disrupt their operations there.\n3\tReturn to Thurindol\tThurindol can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should talk to Thurindol.\n",
[4325]="70042EC2\n1\tDisrupt the forces gathered at Lân Mefam\tLân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin. You should enter the Haradrim camp, Lân Mefam.\n2\tComplete Quest, Lân Mefam: Marksmen\030Complete Quest, Lân Mefam: Mûmakil Feed\030Complete Quest, Lân Mefam: Haradrim Tents\030Complete Quest, Lân Mefam: Half-troll Axes\030Defeat Haradrim Sorcerers (total: 3)\tLân Mefam is located east of Bâr Húrin. You should defeat Haradrim Sorcerers and search for other ways to disrupt their operations there.\n3\tTalk to Anborn\tAnborn can be found in the keep at Bâr Húrin. You should return to Anborn and tell him how you disrupted the Haradrim camp.\n",
[4326]="70066584\n1\tDefeat crebain or ravens around Parth Rest (total: 10)\tFaniel has asked you to defeat crebain around Parth Rest.\n2\tTalk to Faniel in Parth Rest\tYou have done what you can to quell the encroaching crebain. You should report your success to Faniel. Faniel can be found in Parth Rest.\n",
[4327]="7001570F\n1\tPlace stones upon the altars (total: 4)\tThe Ghâsh-hai altars can be found on the bridge-like structures surrounding The Cross-roads of Ash. Gúthi believes the Ghâsh-hai can be convinced to join the forces of Mordor. He wants you to place several stones marked with the Great Eye on the altars near The Cross-roads of Ash.\n2\tTalk to Gúthi at the Cross-roads of Ash\tGúthi is located at the Cross-roads of Ash, in the south-west portion of The Flaming Deeps.\n",
[4328]="700032CA\n1\tDefeat spear-wielding goblins (total: 6)\tSpear-wielding goblins can be found in the north Greenfields. Ponto Hornblower is afraid that he might be attacked from a distance by goblins throwing spears, if the rumours prove true, and has asked you to remove that threat.\n2\tTalk to Ponto Hornblower\tPonto Hornblower is in Brockenborings, near the centre of town. Rumours of goblins in the Greenfields had Ponto Hornblower concerned for his safety and the safety of his sheep. He had asked you to make sure there were no spear-wielding goblins in the fields. You found many, but managed to dispatch them without too much trouble. You should let Ponto know it should be safe for him to return to the Greenfields, though tact may be required to avoid panicking the Shire-folk.\n",
[4329]="7000EECA\n1\tTalk to Leithólf\tForochel lies north of Evendim through Cirith Rhiw, north of Tyrn Fornech. You should start your search in the village of Kauppa-kohta.\n",
[4330]="7006A081\n1\tFind the fishing spot Barhador described\tCatch three fish from the stream just south of where Barhador is camped in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n2\tCatch fresh fish (total: 3)\tCatch three fresh fish at Barhador's recommended fishing spot in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n3\tReturn to Barhador with the fish\tReturn to Barhador at his camp in the Angle of Mitheithel with the three fresh fish you caught.\n",
[4331]="7002C1F8\n1\tSearch the river's edge near Noriel (total: 3)\tEvidence of trespassers can likely be found at the water's edge in the northern part of the road in Thinglad, near where the sentinel Noriel is guarding the road. You should search for evidence of trespassers while Noriel stands guard.\n2\tTell Noriel of the nets you found\tNoriel, sentinel of Thinglad, stands on the road near the edge of Lothlórien. You should tell Noriel of the nets you found.\n3\tSearch nearby for a sign of trespassers\tNoriel has asked you to search the woods nearby for signs of trespassers. You should search the forest floor for anything out of the ordinary.\n4\tBring the horseshoe to Noriel\tNoriel guards the forest edge along the border of Lothlórien. You should bring the horseshoe to Noriel.\n",
[4332]="700321E3\n1\tDefeat the disturbed láthbears (total: 4)\tThe disturbed láthbears can be found in the woods east of Faldham. The disturbed láthbears have grown more aggressive and must be defeated before they can expand towards the village of Faldham.\n2\tCompleted\tThe disturbed láthbears were unable to harm the people of Faldham in their aggression, due to your efforts in defeating them.\n",
[4333]="70022B3A\n1\tTend the open graves (total: 4)\tDisturbed graves can be found deep within the Flooded Wing of the Great Barrow.\n",
[4334]="70015E04\n1\tTalk to Lengliel at Echad Eregion\tLengliel is at Echad Eregion, south-east of Gwingris. Calelloth has asked you to deliver a letter to Lengliel regarding the half-orcs and worms.\n",
[4335]="70041A4A\n1\tSearch for Jajax's brother\tJajax's brother can be found somewhere in Hata Kebir. Jajax has begged your aid in finding his brother who he believes is among the forces at Hata Kebir.\n",
[4336]="7003FFFE\n1\tDefeat sappers (total: 4)\tThe sappers must be defeated.\n",
[4337]="70062D1A\n1\tDefeat avanc near Fangsettle (total: 8)\tThere is an avanc nesting ground in the Wadewater west of Lhan Garan named Fangsettle. Slay avanc near Fangsettle.\n2\tTalk to Culhuc\tCulhuc is tending the community oven in Lhan Garan. Talk to Culhuc.\n",
[4338]="700611EF\n1\tCollect wolf-weed (total: 6)\tWolf-weed can be found along the wood's edge north of Tighfield. Collect wolf-weed.\n2\tTalk to Henepa Twistknot\tHenepa Twistknot can be found tending bar at the The Elbow's Bend in the village of Tighfield. Return to Henepa Twistknot.\n",
[4339]="70068C01\n1\tTalk to Kina in the Gut\tShikavi has asked you to try and reach Kina and help him see the realities of pirate life.\n2\tDefeat Kina's guards\tKina has run away disinterested in what you have to say leaving you to deal with his friends.\n3\tTalk to Shikavi\tYou handled Kina's supposed friends, but they ran away in the process. You should tell Shikavi.\n",
[4340]="70068C03\n1\tConfront Hûmaraz\tShikavi has asked you to appeal to the authority of the captain of the crew of which Kina pretends to be a member. Captain Hûmaraz can be found on the south-east end of Lower Ward.\n2\tTalk to Shikavi\tYou have slain Hûmaraz, but Kina ran away again, his feelings hurt by what once was his idol. You should check in with Shikavi. Shikavi can be found outside of the Black Anchor Tavern.\n",
[4341]="7001BA87\n1\tTalk to Candaith at his camp\tCandaith is at his camp on the western side of Weathertop. The hunters do not know the name Candaith, but they have seen the makings of a camp at the western foot of Weathertop.\n",
[4342]="70035210\n1\tTear down enemy flags and investigate homes\tEnemy flags can be found outside of the homes in Byre Tor. You should destroy enemy flags and search the homes for survivors of the White Hand assault.\n2\tDestroy enemy flags outside of homes (total: 5)\030Investigate the first home\030Investigate the second home\030Investigate the third home\030Investigate the fourth home\030Investigate the fifth home\tEnemy flags can be found outside of the homes in Byre Tor. You should destroy Enemy flags and search the homes for survivors of the White Hand assault.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have investigated many homes in Byre Tor, but they are all empty. It would appear that there are no survivors.\n",
[4343]="7002EF54\n1\tDefeat swert-hounds throughout the East Wall (total: 6)\tSwert-hounds can be found throughout the East Wall. Cúfaron has asked you to hunt some of the swert-hounds that haunt the East Wall.\n2\tTalk to Cúfaron\tCúfaron is at Hestil's camp on Parth Galen. You have defeated many swert-hounds and should now return to Cúfaron as he asked.\n",
[4344]="7001AD24\n1\tCollect war-collars (total: 12)\tWargs can be found roaming throughout Taur Morvith. Iavassúl has asked you to hunt down the Wargs roaming Taur Morvith and collect their war-collars as trophies.\n2\tBring the collars to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch\tIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith. You should return the war-collars to Iavassúl.\n",
[4345]="700411C7\n1\tSpeak with Ransroth\tTalk to Ransroth\n",
